SDUSD::notifyRewardAmount
├── given PAUSE_TYPE is paused
│   └── it should revert with IsPaused
└── given PAUSE_TYPE is not paused
    ├── when caller is not the configured rewarder
    │   └── it should revert with SDUSDNotRewarder
    └── when caller is the configured rewarder
        ├── when the previous reward period is active
        │   └── it should revert with SDUSDRewardPeriodNotFinished
        ├── when address(1) holds fewer shares than seedShares
        │   ├── it should revert with SDUSDNotSeeded
        │   └── when user-owned total supply exceeds seedShares
        │       └── it should still revert with SDUSDNotSeeded
        ├── when all real stakers have exited and only seed shares remain
        │   └── it should revert with SDUSDNoActiveStakers
        ├── when amount is zero
        │   └── it should revert with SDUSDZeroAmount
        ├── when the rewarder has insufficient DUSD balance or allowance
        │   ├── it should revert with the underlying token transfer error
        │   └── it should leave all reward accounting unchanged
        └── when the previous period has finished, amount is non-zero, and real stakers exist
            ├── it should pull exactly amount DUSD from the rewarder
            ├── it should increase accountedAssets by amount
            ├── it should set rewardsForPeriod to amount
            ├── it should set periodStart to the current timestamp
            ├── it should set rewardPeriodFinish to periodStart plus rewardDuration
            ├── it should leave total supply and all share balances unchanged
            ├── it should exclude the new reward amount from totalAssets at periodStart
            ├── it should preserve the exchange rate at periodStart without an immediate reward spike
            ├── it should emit RewardAdded with amount and rewardPeriodFinish
            ├── when block timestamp equals the previous rewardPeriodFinish
            │   ├── it should start the new reward period
            │   └── it should preserve the fully vested exchange rate when the new period starts
            └── when a completed period already has rewardsForPeriod recorded
                ├── it should replace the period reward state without removing previously accounted rewards
                └── it should not spike the exchange rate when replacing the period state
